# smoke_search_batch — dev-only MEMORY + TIMING smoke for the campaign search
# path: the fixed_probabilistic design at the campaign N (300 x 10 yr, draw 0)
# evaluated through Borg workers WITH the realization batch the production
# env files set (150), on one wholenode node at the production packing
# density (128 ranks/node). Submitted via workflow/submit_search_memory_smoke.sh,
# which sizes the allocation (1 node, 127 ranks = 1 controller + 2 islands x
# (62 workers + 1 master)), starts a node-memory sampler, and uses the tiny
# `smoke` MOEA config (200 NFE/island -> ~3 evaluation waves).
#
# Answers, before any production search: (i) node RSS at 128 ranks with the
# batch set (target <= 217 GB); (ii) warm evaluation time at N=300 batched
# (expected ~540 s = 173.8 s x 2.84 x 1.09); (iii) that the batched path runs
# inside a Borg search at all (it has only ever run in step-09 re-evals).
#
# PREREQUISITE: fixed_probabilistic staged at N=300 (steps 02 -> 04, draw 0).

NYCOPT_SCENARIO_DESIGN="fixed_probabilistic"
NYCOPT_MOEA_CONFIG="smoke"
NYCOPT_SEARCH_REALIZATION_BATCH=150

NYCOPT_FORMULATIONS="ffmp"
NYCOPT_SALINITY_ON=0
NYCOPT_TEMPERATURE_ON=0
NYCOPT_NYC_NJ_DEMAND_SOURCE="constant_max"
NYCOPT_OBJECTIVES="nyc_delivery_reliability_weekly,nyc_delivery_deficit_cvar90_pct,montague_flow_reliability_weekly,montague_flow_deficit_cvar90_pct,trenton_flow_reliability_weekly,downstream_flood_exceedance_minor,nyc_storage_p5_pct,nj_delivery_reliability_weekly"
NYCOPT_CLUSTER="anvil"
